I believe that the owner of the castle is Croesus -- he is one of the
inhabitants of the castle, and he wields a mean two-handed sword.

He is the only character in Nethack I am aware of who is a historical
character (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Croesus). He was a king in what
is now modern Turkey. He went to war with the Persians under Cyrus the
Great, on the strength of a prophecy that if he did so he would destroy
a mighty empire.  He lost the battle and his kingdom was conquered by
the Persians.  He spent the rest of his life a prisoner at the Persian
court.  Herodotus tells us he sent his chains back to the oracle with a
comment on the value of prophecies, and got the answer back that it had
been a true prophecy. He HAD destroyed a mighty kingdom -- his own.

The histories don't tell us whether Croesus had multiple dragons
guarding his stronghold (at Sardis). I somehow doubt it :).

